Thank you!

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.380
It's pretty lively over at their stage.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:09.880
Wouldn't it have been best to have
Eiko sing as scheduled, after all?

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.210
There is no cause for concern.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.920
Allow me to show you
Stratagem Seven of the Thirty-Six:

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.080
"Create something from nothing."

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.710
You guys are the best!

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:25.420
<i>The truth is, today's basically a throwaway match.</i>

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.420
<i>This'll be an easy win for us.</i>

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.420
Uh, I'd like to a make an announcement-

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:38.540
What a racket!

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:39.540
They're killing the vibe!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:40.880
<i>Is their equipment working again?</i>

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.080
<i>Now of all times?</i>

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.830
<i>Alright, here I go!</i>

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:56.540
Hey!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.040
Be crazy for me

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.330
Make me shine on you

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.460
You're gonna see me

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.750
When you hear my music

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.460
I'll be there for you

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:07.210
No matter where you go

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:10.380
How do you see me from your point of view?

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.290
Wow!

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.580
She's actually good.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:10.790
Who is she?

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.460
I steal your heart

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.000
Play "Mid Day"!

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.080
"Mid Day"!

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.920
"Mid Day"! "Mid Day"! "Mid Day"!

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:16.080
I'll take you higher

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.960
Are you crazy for me?

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.540
<i>"Mid Day" is...</i>

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:23.830
"Mid Day"! "Mid Day"! "Mid Day"!

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.330
I'll take you higher

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.580
Are you crazy for me?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.080
We'll play "Mid Day" at our solo concert tomorrow,

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.330
Let me go my own way

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.670
so today we'll perform "Rain Fall."

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.670
‘Cause I believe you

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.880
"Mid Day" is their only song I know.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:32.330
Mikansei no mama ja iya na no
I don't like it being left unfinished<b></b>

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.540
Wanna check out that stage?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.750
I'm kinda curious.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.380
Don't let it fade away

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.250
Oh, I know this song! I love it!

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.960
I'll make it come true

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.790
EIKO? Never heard of her.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:39.210
Demo tsukamu ni wa tarinai no
But it is not enough to grab onto<b></b>

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.000
But I'm diggin' it!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:42.460
Kanousei nara mugendai
The possibilities are infinite<b></b>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:46.290
Kakete mite, uragiranai
Bet on me, I won't betray you<b></b>

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.750
<i>Oh my god!</i>

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.290
<i>This feels awesome!</i>

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:49.250
Sono omoi ni wa kotaetai
I want to respond to that feeling<b></b>

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.330
What's going on?

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.250
That "Create something from nothing" stratagem...

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:52.960
Kimi no koe de, bring it to me
With your voice, bring it to me<b></b>

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:51.290
What'd you do?

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.880
"Create something from nothing"...

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.040
In other words, make it appear that something
which doesn't exist in fact does.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.630
Be crazy for me

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.880
Make me shine on you

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.790
You mean how you faked the equipment issues, right?

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.000
You're gonna see me

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.380
When you hear my music

00:13:58.790 --> 00:13:59.830
I get that much,

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.920
but why'd the crowd make their way over here?

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.920
I'll be there for you

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.960
No matter where you go

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.250
I predicted that, as a first-time performer,

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:05.960
Eiko would be assigned this location.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:11.830
After which, I researched Jet Jacket,
who were set to go on at the same time, in detail.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.330
Their vocalist is high-strung and deliberate,

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.920
and he easily gets a sore throat.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.290
What do you base that on?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.000
Physiognomy.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.920
And I only became more sure of it
when I met him earlier.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.170
In addition, they have an important concert tomorrow.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.170
Their competition today was an unknown
with limited popularity.

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:30.580
What's more, she was having issues.

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:33.130
Well then, what was his frame of mind?

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:36.130
He'd take it easy in preparation for tomorrow.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.290
Exactly.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:42.170
Moreover, their signature song, "Mid Day,"
is tough on the throat.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:46.290
He never sings it two days in a row,
as his vocal chords require rest.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:47.960
Ah, I see.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:51.500
That's when you deploy the flashy lighting
and a hit cover song that fires people up.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.500
All but their most loyal fans will head over here.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.710
It's perfect!

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:58.880
Er, wait, there was a non-zero chance that
we could've ended up in a different location.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.420
It seems the Will of Heaven favors Eiko.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.540
As a result, I had no need to use THAT stratagem.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.380
<i>Another stratagem?</i>

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.580
<i>Just how far ahead can this guy see?</i>

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.630
<i>Kongming, are you...</i>

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.540
<i>the real Kongming?!</i>

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.130
All right, let's put on the finishing touches.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.790
"Finishing touches"?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.710
What else is up your sleeve?!

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.040
Cheers!

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.790
Go on and have one.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.380
Don’t startle me like that.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:29.830
Just giving the fans some freebies, eh?

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.330
I do have some regrets.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.630
What about?

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:36.250
Once, when Cao Cao's army came after us,

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.130
we were forced to flee with common folk in tow.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.250
The prior night, I'd been invited to a drinking party,

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:48.000
but on account of being busy,
I coldly turned down the offer.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:54.080
On reflection, that was a farewell drink for soldiers
who were prepared to meet their end...

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:59.250
They all laid down their lives on the battlefield
so that the common folk could escape.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:05.790
Back then, why did I not share
so much as a single drink with them?

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.670
Why, I ask?

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.670
Kongming...

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:15.790
"For all things are born of the tangible,
but the tangible arises from nothing."

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.040
This, too, is "creating something from nothing."

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.130
Life is but a fleeting moment.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.960
Let us enjoy ourselves.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.670
Yeah, with the best music and liquor.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.380
Perfection.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.500
What's up, everybody?!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.250
Put your lights up!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.290
It seems Eiko's really gained some confidence.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.380
And that was exactly my aim for this event.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.380
What?

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:42.080
Among the fifteen rules for a commander
is found "humility."

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:45.000
That is, conducting oneself with modesty.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.080
However, I dare say Eiko has too much humility.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.580
Her low self-assessment holds her back.

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.000
A victory on unfamiliar ground...

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.540
I suspect she will take to heart

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:59.130
a successful experience as intense as this one.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.580
I see.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.210
So that's why you wanted her to perform at a festival.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.080
You put a lot of thought into it.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.210
And there is one more reason...

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.790
Should my prediction prove correct...

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.880
And here they come.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.630
I'd like a word with EIKO's manager.

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.080
Huh? You guys-

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.670
I shall hear you out.

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:21.750
Hey now, Kongming!

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.500
You needn't worry.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:26.380
I'm accustomed to such things on the battlefield.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:28.540
I have some skill in this area.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:32.830
You play dirty!

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.790
Oh my, whatever do you mean?

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.000
Don't play dumb!

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.080
You blasted out sound the second
I started addressing the audience!

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.130
Like hell your equipment started working just then!

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.580
Did you even get permission to put
lights in the tree like that?!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.670
You faked your equipment issues
to get us to let our guard down.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:48.670
Isn't that right?!

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:49.960
Let your guard down?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.170
Oh...

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.170
We were working frantically over here.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:56.130
No such thought even crossed my mind.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.000
What? I hate this damn guy!
Can I slug 'im?

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.330
Don't make a scene!

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:03.000
If that's the way you feel...

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.460
Ta-da!

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.460
<b>TA-DA!</b>

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.540
What's that?

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:11.790
I've heard that your vocalist has been
battling issues with his throat.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:19.080
It’s a throat-soothing decoction that
messengers carried with them in the past.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.250
If you're so inclined, please try some.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.880
Like hell I'd drink that!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.130
Don’t screw with me!

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.330
Gimme that.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.460
Hey!

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.580
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:35.420
Hurry and spit it out! C'mon!

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.500
So...

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.420
So soothing!

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.420
WHAT?!

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:40.580
This stuff's crazy!

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:43.630
It tastes like crap but really opens up your throat!
Go on and try some.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.830
No friggin' way!

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.040
Gimme a sip.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.250
Wait!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.460
Hold up, I said.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.250
Actually, it's not bad.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:52.750
Right?
Actually, it's not bad.<b></b>

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:53.250
Right?
You outta your damn minds?!<b></b>

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.380
You outta your damn minds?!

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.380
Drink some.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.250
Cut the crap! Why should I?

00:18:57.250 --> 00:19:00.130
Well, you're unstoppable when
your throat's in good shape.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:02.250
Here.

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:05.830
No harm in trying.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.170
Just get it over with.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.540
It's not good to be picky!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.750
You idiots.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.170
I've been seeing an actual doctor, you know?

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.380
C'mon already!

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:20.000
<b>soothing~</b>

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.710
So soothing!

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.080
The discomfort in my throat's completely gone!

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.580
What the hell's in this stuff?

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:30.380
I've uploaded the recipe to Cookingpad,
so please have a look.

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.040
It's got a crap ton of reviews!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.880
Since "Mid Day"...

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:38.420
I'm of the opinion that your songs after you started
using DAW software are also wonderful,

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:43.540
but I must say I preferred your wild,
first-year festival performance.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.790
So, could please I get your autographs?

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:48.210
Had you displayed the same vigor you did back then,

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:51.210
I suspect no one would've left your performance.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.630
Shut up!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.920
You really are obnoxious.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.040
It's not like I've forgotten, okay?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.880
Oh? About what exactly?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.830
That it's not the size of the stage that matters.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.630
That EIKO girl...

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:09.170
She's actually not bad.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.830
Thank you.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:14.000
That said, if we ever go up against each other again,

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.750
it's payback time!

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:19.880
Also...

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.380
about that medicine...

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.880
Thank you.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:28.380
Man, I actually really like that dude.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.420
Stop your fanboying!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.250
You like him even more than I do!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:30.670
Kongming!
You like him even more than I do!<b></b>

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:31.670
Kongming!
Shut up!<b></b>

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:33.880
Are you sure that was wise?

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:36.170
Showing humanity to an adversary like that?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.380
It is fine.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.330
Appreciating one's enemy is part of
having a command of battle.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:43.670
Like how Guan Yu raised his hat to Zhang Liao.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:45.580
Oh, the siege of Lu Bu's castle!

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:49.500
Nevertheless, I am glad these are peaceful times.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.000
If times had not changed,

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:57.420
I would have been forced to line up
the severed heads of those three on stage.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:58.630
That's horrifying!

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:01.170
I love you guys!

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:03.170
Thank you!

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:09.000
I'm back!

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
Huh? They're not here.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.000
Where'd you run off to? Jeez!

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.040
We had a little business.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.580
Great work tonight, Eiko.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:23.420
How was I?

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:24.830
You were splendid.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:28.710
I wasn't sure how it'd pan out at first,
but I felt great up on stage!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.540
As a rookie singer,

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:34.460
it would be understandable for you to have felt
a sense of alienation at a festival like this.

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:36.380
But at the same time,

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.630
it provided an opportunity to have your music
heard by a great many people.

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:44.380
I believed that you could surely pull it off, Eiko.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:49.250
I want even way more people to hear me sing!

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:53.460
I will continue to put my body and soul
into supporting you.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.670
Thanks!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.380
Oh?

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:02.330
It would seem the one we're really after
has been caught in our net.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:11.580
<b>Kongming Learns of the Right Path to Take</b>

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:14.920
Hey DJ

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:18.830
Do it, yeah yeah yeah, that superb-feeling

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:22.750
Needle, drop it, blast the sound, party night

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:26.630
Let's drink, alright alright alright, let's all dance!

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:32.920
Hip-pop people, play that miracle number

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:40.040
Yo! Music that we share in an era like this

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:41.960
We want to search for it, a globe that spins

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:43.920
Wavering, unstable lives

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:45.750
That's why we emphasize balance

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:48.040
Not everything is great, so I can try my best!

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:49.630
Kick the worst of days

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:51.500
Click the restart button!

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:53.290
DJ, play it! Now, trip

00:22:53.290 --> 00:23:03.000
Let's groove to the hip beat and shake our feeling bodies

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:08.830
Hey DJ, butt in, yeah yeah yeah, that superb-feeling

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:12.670
Wave, ride it and fly off, funky night

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:16.540
Let's drink, alright alright alright, let's all dance!

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:24.000
Hip-pop people, a miracle number until the morn

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:30.210
Hey DJ, do it, yeah yeah yeah

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:34.000
Let's drink, alright alright alright

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:37.750
Hey DJ, do it, yeah yeah yeah
